'''''Cymbidium iridioides''''', commonly known as the '''Iris-Like Cymbidium'''<ref>{{Cite web |title=IOSPE PHOTOS |url=http://www.orchidspecies.com/cymiridiodes.htm |access-date=2023-06-24 |website=www.orchidspecies.com}}</ref> is a [[species]] of [[Cymbidium|boat orchid]]. It is a [[pseudobulb]]ous [[epiphyte]] found from [[Himalaya]] to south-central [[China]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Cymbidium iridioides D.Don {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:625056-1 |access-date=2023-06-24 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref>

== Distribution and habitat ==
''Cymbidium iridioides'' is native to [[Assam]], south-central China, Himalaya, [[Myanmar]], [[Nepal]], [[Tibet]], [[Vietnam]].<ref name=":0" />

Under natural conditions, it is found on trees or rocks, and on shaded [[cliff]]s at elevations of 900–2800 meters from [[sea level]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Cymbidium iridioides in Flora of China @ efloras.org |url=http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=2&taxon_id=242421731 |access-date=2023-06-24 |website=www.efloras.org}}</ref>

== Description ==
It is a pseudobulbous epiphyte. The pseudobulbs are {{cvt|4|to|11|cm}} long and {{cvt|2|to|5|cm}} wide, and are ellipsoid-ovoid to narrowly ovoid.

The flowers are {{cvt|9|to|10|cm}} in diameter, the [[Pedicel (botany)|pedicel]] and [[Ovary (botany)|ovary]] are {{cvt|40|to|45|mm}}. The [[sepals]] and the [[petals]] are yellowish green, with 7–9 brownish to reddish brown longitudinal stripes. The lip is yellowish, with red or brown stripes on the lateral lobes and on the mid-lobe. The sepals are narrowly obovate-oblong, and are {{cvt|37|to|45|mm}} ×  {{cvt|12|to|15|mm}}. The petals are slightly falcate, and are {{cvt|35|to|46|mm}} × {{cvt|7|to|9|mm}}

